For invalidFarmerTotalReturns422: call WaterService.billFarmer(new BigDecimal("-1")) expect ApiException with 422; new BigDecimal("1.0001") → 422. Also valid: billFarmer(150) = 350.00; billFarmer(100.005)=200.02; billFarmer(0)=0.00.

Helper methods:

```java
private long createWindow(String planned) — channel unique per call
private String submit(long windowId, String userId, String amount, String actor)
private void approve(String allocationKey)
private JsonNode transfer(String source, String target, String actor, String amount?) — target's amount defines transfer; submit target with desired amount first.
private JsonNode settle(long windowId, int expectedStatus) — POST settlements {requestId}
private JsonNode reconcile(long windowId, long expectedVersion, int expectedStatus)
```

For concurrency: call waterService.reconcile(key, windowId, 1L) directly.

Note expectedSettlementVersion is Long in DTO; service signature takes Long.

Test: concurrent reconciles — both with expected 1. One gets 200, other 409 VERSION_CONFLICT. Then list versions: size 2 (v1 + one new).

Let me now also think about the GET /settlements response shape assertions: currentVersion, currentNetReceivable, settlements array with version/totalAmount/diffAmount/lines.

Amounts format: fmtAmount → "350.00". Lines volume: fmt → "150". totalAmount "350.00", diffAmount "-60.00".

Now write the file in segments. Segment 1: package/imports/class/fields/helpers (~120 lines). Segment 2: main-flow tests. Segment 3: idempotency + concurrency + unit tests.

